    {
      "id": "riesz-map-conjugate-linear-operator-example",
      "type": "example",
      "regions": [
        [
          243,
          80,
          415,
          955,
          685
        ]
      ],
      "en": "The Riesz representation theorem states that every Hilbert space $H$ is isometric to its dual space $H^*$. In Remark~\\ref{rem:riesz-mappings} we constructed the map $A_H:H^*\\to H$ that, for every linear functional $l\\in H^*$, gives the unique element $x=A_H(l)\\in H$ such that\\[l(y)=(x,y)\\quad\\text{for all }y\\in H.\\]Note that the operator $A_H$ is actually \\emph{conjugate linear}; i.e., $A_H(\\alpha l)=\\bar\\alpha A_H(l)$. The operator is bounded; the Riesz representation theorem assures us that its norm is $1$.",
      "zh": "Riesz 表示定理断言, 每个 Hilbert 空间 $H$ 都与其对偶空间 $H^*$ 等距. 在 Remark~\\ref{rem:riesz-mappings} 中构造了映射 $A_H:H^*\\to H$, 它对每个线性泛函 $l\\in H^*$ 给出唯一元素 $x=A_H(l)\\in H$, 使\\[l(y)=(x,y)\\quad\\text{for all }y\\in H.\\]注意, 算子 $A_H$ 实际上是\\emph{共轭线性的}; 即 $A_H(\\alpha l)=\\bar\\alpha A_H(l)$. 该算子有界; Riesz 表示定理保证其范数为 $1$.",
      "label": "ex:riesz-map-conjugate-linear-operator",
      "minimum_heading_lines": 4,
      "render_role": "example",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 243,
          "printed_page": 233,
          "bbox": [
